Leftovers on the plate: a couple of tomato slices (about 40 g), a small piece of salmon or similar (about 8 g), a bread crumb (about 3 g), and plastic wrap, which is not food. Total is roughly 50 g.

Energy: tomato is about 18 kcal per 100 g, so 40 g gives about 7 kcal. The salmon piece is about 8 g at roughly 2 kcal/g in smoked or cured form, so about 15 kcal at most; at a more typical 1.8 kcal/g it is about 14 kcal. The bread crumb is about 8 kcal. The total is about 29 kcal, which I round to 28.

